// Renovate (GitHub App, https://github.com/apps/renovate): a pull request for each new release of
// what Speech Language Switcher builds on, plus the "Dependency Dashboard" issue listing what is
// open. Its own pull request: Bun (packageManager in package.json, read by Renovate's npm manager,
// the Bun of CI). The VS Code API (engines.vscode, @types/vscode and the README badge) is never
// updated by Renovate, the same as in firsttris/vscode-jest-runner.
// Everything else (the other packages, the actions, the images) comes with the shared settings of
// firsttris/workflows (renovate/default.json5): minor and patch updates once a month in one pull
// request that merges itself when CI is green, majors on request in the dashboard.
// Check with `bunx --package renovate renovate-config-validator .github/renovate.json5`.
{
  $schema: "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",
  extends: ["github>firsttris/workflows//renovate/default.json5"],
  customManagers: [
    {
      // engines.vscode, from the same releases as @types/vscode: vsce refuses a package whose
      // @types/vscode is newer than engines.vscode, so both take the same version
      customType: "regex",
      managerFilePatterns: ["/^package\\.json$/"],
      matchStrings: ['"engines": \\{\\s*"vscode": "\\^(?<currentValue>\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+)"'],
      depNameTemplate: "vscode-engine",
      packageNameTemplate: "@types/vscode",
      datasourceTemplate: "npm",
    },
    {
      // The "VS Code x.y.z+" badge of the README
      customType: "regex",
      managerFilePatterns: ["/^README\\.md$/"],
      matchStrings: ["badge/VS%20Code-(?<currentValue>\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+)\\+-blue"],
      depNameTemplate: "vscode-badge",
      packageNameTemplate: "@types/vscode",
      datasourceTemplate: "npm",
    },
  ],
  packageRules: [
    {
      // The lowest VS Code the extension runs on, ^1.100.0 like Jest Runner. Raising it shuts out
      // every editor still on an older one (VSCodium, Cursor, Windsurf lag behind VS Code): Jest
      // Runner no longer showed up in Cursor's extension search with a newer engine. So Renovate
      // never proposes it, not even in the Dependency Dashboard (#17 raised it to ^1.144.0 and was
      // closed). Only when a newer API is really needed: set `enabled: true` here, or raise
      // engines.vscode, @types/vscode and the README badge by hand, after checking the forks'
      // VS Code version.
      matchManagers: ["npm", "custom.regex"],
      matchPackageNames: ["@types/vscode"],
      enabled: false,
      rangeStrategy: "bump",
      groupName: "VS Code engine",
      commitMessageTopic: "VS Code engine",
      dependencyDashboardApproval: true,
      prBodyNotes: [
        "`engines.vscode`, `@types/vscode` and the README badge move together (`vsce package` fails when `@types/vscode` is newer than `engines.vscode`). Before merging: is this API really needed? Check which VS Code version the forks on Open VSX are based on (VSCodium, Cursor, Windsurf); users on an older one get no more updates. Then `bun run package`, and try the .vsix of this PR's CI.",
      ],
      schedule: ["at any time"],
      automerge: false,
    },
    {
      // packageManager in package.json: setup-bun's bun-version-file in ci.yml
      matchPackageNames: ["bun"],
      groupName: "Bun",
      sourceUrl: "https://github.com/oven-sh/bun",
      prBodyNotes: [
        "`packageManager` in package.json is the Bun of CI: it installs the packages (`bun.lock`), runs Biome and `tsc` and packages the `.vsix` (`vsce package --no-dependencies`). Check that `ci.yml` stays green, compare `unzip -l` of the `.vsix` artifact with the last release, and run `bun install` locally if `bun.lock` changes.",
      ],
      schedule: ["at any time"],
      automerge: false,
      dependencyDashboardApproval: false,
    },
  ],
}
